# A form can be `reduce`'s `init:` without parentheses. Subtle: the inner
# form has a lambda whose body stops at the outer `with`, so this reads
# `reduce xs init: (reduce xs with times) with plus`: the product 6 seeds a
# sum, giving 6 + 1 + 2 + 3.
#= {result: 12, inputs: {xs: [1, 2, 3]}}
reduce xs init: reduce xs with fn acc, x -> acc * x with fn acc, x -> acc + x
